Q: React native Android - Embedding React native into standalone Android App A: <p>Add the RN project in <code>settings.gradle</code></p>
<pre><code>include(&quot;:rnandroid&quot;)
project(&quot;:rnandroid&quot;).projectDir = file(&quot;rnandroid/android&quot;)
</code></pre>
<p>Create a task in <code>app/build.gradle</code></p>
<pre><code>tasks.register(&quot;generateRnAutolinking&quot;) {
    dependsOn(&quot;:rnandroid:app:generateAutolinkingPackageList&quot;)
    doLast {
        copy {
            from(&quot;$rootDir/rnandroid/android/build/generated&quot;)
            into(&quot;$rootDir/build/generated&quot;)
        }
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>Make it run automatically when pressing <strong>Run App</strong></p>
<pre><code>preBuild.dependsOn(&quot;generateRnAutolinking&quot;)
</code></pre>
<p>Now Android Studio Run App will auto-run autolinking, copy files, and then build.</p>
